OL,3,GNEWSAMosaic fragment 'thought lost' to
OL,4,Ago on display
OL,5,
OL,6,FStaff at a museum say they are
OL,7,F"delighted" a fragment from a long-lost
OL,8,F2nd Century Roman mosaic of sea
OL,9,Fcreatures that was unearthed 243 years
OL,10,Fago has been loaned to them.
OL,12,FThe mosaic, which will be on display at
OL,13,FCoronium Museum, in Cirencester,
OL,14,FGloucestershire, was discovered under
OL,15,Fthe foundations of nearby Gloucester
OL,16,FHouse, on Dyer Street in 1783.
OL,18,FThe original mosaic depicted sea
OL,19,Fcreatures including fish, an eel and a
OL,20,Fcrab, alongside mythological figures
OL,21,Fincluding swimming cupids and a
OL,22,Fsea-leopard.
OL,23,APub: 31-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
